@anon.152f57749fcdf0a673d809c4f4545e7f.689 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [949 x i8] }> <{ [949 x i8] c"The destination the link points to.\0A\0A- To link to web pages, `dest` should be a valid URL string. If the URL\0A  is in the `mailto:` or `tel:` scheme and the `body` parameter is\0A  omitted, the email address or phone number will be the link's body,\0A  without the scheme.\0A\0A- To link to another part of the document, `dest` can take one of three\0A  forms:\0A  - A [label] attached to an element. If you also want automatic text\0A    for the link based on the element, consider using a\0A    [reference]($ref) instead.\0A\0A  - A [`location`] (typically retrieved from [`here`], [`locate`] or\0A    [`query`]).\0A\0A  - A dictionary with a `page` key of type [integer]($int) and `x` and\0A    `y` coordinates of type [length]. Pages are counted from one, and\0A    the coordinates are relative to the page's top left corner.\0A\0A```example\0A= Introduction <intro>\0A#link(\22mailto:hello@typst.app\22) \\\0A#link(<intro>)[Go to intro] \\\0A#link((page: 1, x: 0pt, y: 0pt))[\0A  Go to top\0A]\0A```" }>, align 1
